/* AppGrid.jsx — the App Grid (App Menu launcher overlay).

   Task 2 of the App Grid v2 build plan builds only the L1 atoms below —
   `AppGridTab` and `AppGridTile` — as FILE-PRIVATE functions. Neither is
   exposed on `window` yet; that `Object.assign(window, { AppGrid })` line
   is added in Task 4 once the full public `AppGrid` overlay composes these
   atoms (via the L2 molecules built in Task 3). Do not compose either
   function from a page or another file until then.

   Source of truth: docs/superpowers/notes/2026-07-06-app-grid-figma-specs.md
   — Section A (AppGridTabs, node 1:4544) for AppGridTab, Section C
   (AppsGridTiles, node 1:5101) for AppGridTile. Figma file GskDcyTOG8bI4adjHmnqu7.

   Deps: Icons.jsx (Icon), Primitives.jsx (Avatar — reserved for a later
   molecule task; not used directly by these two atoms), tokens.js (ARC.*).
   The folder glyph is the complete static folder asset —
   assets/icons/folder.svg — referenced via <img>, NOT an Icons.jsx
   component. It is a two-path SVG (dark tab #444F5C behind + gray body
   #D4D5D6 in front, with the Figma mirror baked in), so the whole folder
   silhouette renders faithfully; the earlier appGridFolderTab.svg (the
   dark accent ALONE, composited over a plain square) was replaced because
   it showed a solid dark block instead of a thin folder tab. */

